means:

(i) A person named as executor in a will;

(ii) A person serving as personal representative after judicial or administrative probate;

(iii) A legatee in being, whether the legatee’s interest is vested or contingent, except that a legatee whose interest has been fully paid or fully adeemed ceases to be an "interested person" on receipt of payment or notice of the ademption;

(iv) An heir even if the decedent dies testate, except that an heir of a testate decedent ceases to be an "interested person" when the register has given notice pursuant to § 2–210 or § 5–403(a) of this article;

(v) An heir or legatee whose interest is contingent solely on whether some other heir or legatee survives the decedent by a stated period if the other heir or legatee has died within that period;

(vi) A surviving spouse who has timely filed an election to take an elective share under § 3–403 of this article, except that the surviving spouse ceases to be an "interested person" on the election being withdrawn or ruled ineffective by a court of competent jurisdiction; or

(vii) A person who timely files a petition to caveat under § 5–207 of this article, except that the person ceases to be an "interested person" once the caveat proceeding has been disposed of.

